# Backend Standards (Python FastAPI)

## Tech Stack
- Python 3.11+
- FastAPI
- Uvicorn (ASGI server)
- Pydantic v2 (Data validation)
- Image Processing: Use `Pillow` (PIL) for image handling.
- AI Vision: Pass image buffers directly to Gemini using the modern `google-genai` SDK multimedia format.

## AI Configuration
- Use the official Google GenAI SDK (`google-genai`).
- Target model: `gemini-1.5-flash`.
- Keep AI prompt templates isolated in a `backend/app/prompts.py` file.

## Architecture & Conventions
- Structure: `main.py` -> `routes/` -> `services/` (AI logic).
- Always use typed definitions and Pydantic schemas for request/response payloads.
- Use explicit `try/except` blocks for handling AI API call failures and return clear HTTP 500 status codes if the AI fails.

## Testing Standards
- Use `pytest` for all backend tests.
- Place all tests inside a `/backend/tests/` directory mirroring the app structure.

